{
  "version": 2,
  "description": "technical-scope.md §7.9.6: shared test vectors for PriceCalculator. Used by the PHP test suite (tests/Unit/Tax/Domain/PriceCalculatorVectorsTest.php); the web app and any e-commerce integration should validate against the same vectors, or call POST /api/v1/companies/{companyId}/calculate directly with the same 'input' shape. A changed or new vector is a fiscal change: it needs 🧑 owner review before merge (docs/plans/phase-2.md task 2.1). Rounding mode is ROUND_HALF_UP (technical-scope.md §7.9.2) throughout; 'cascading-percentage-discounts' and 'cascading-plus-fixed' each land on an exact half-cent and are the vectors that actually pin the mode down (banker's rounding would fail both). Non-PHP consumers (the web app, e-commerce integrations) MUST NOT use native float arithmetic to reproduce these — JavaScript's `(x*rate/100).toFixed(2)` and `Math.round(x*100)/100` both get at least one of the two half-cent vectors wrong. Use an arbitrary-precision decimal library (decimal.js or big.js) configured for ROUND_HALF_UP.",
  "known_gaps": [
    "Credit notes / negative amounts: out of scope for PriceCalculator itself until docs/plans/phase-2.md task 2.7 (credit notes). No vector here uses a negative quantity or amount.",
    "No vector combines a fixed-amount global discount with uneven line amounts (global discounts are percentage-only per current input shape — see 'global-discount-with-line-discounts' for the largest-remainder case, which needs a line-level discount to force genuine sub-6dp remainder distribution)."
  ],
  "vectors": [
    {
      "name": "simple-net",
      "notes": "Baseline: no discounts, single line, single tax rate.",
      "input": {
        "pricing_mode": "net",
        "rounding_method": "per_line",
        "date": "2026-01-01",
        "global_discount_percent": null,
        "lines": [
          { "quantity": "2", "unit_price": "50.00", "tax_region": "PT", "tax_code": "NOR" }
        ]
      },
      "expected": {
        "lines": [
          { "line_amount_before_discounts": "100.000000", "discount_amount": "0.000000", "settlement_amount": "0.000000", "net_amount": "100.00", "gross_amount": "123.00", "tax_amount": "23.00", "tax_region": "PT", "tax_code": "NOR", "tax_percentage": "23.00" }
        ],
        "tax_summary": [
          { "tax_region": "PT", "tax_code": "NOR", "tax_percentage": "23.00", "taxable_base": "100.00", "tax_amount": "23.00" }
